    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0bf92683_8221811f",
        "filename": "include/trace/events/vendor_hook.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-27T16:38:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No strong opinion really. It just felt a little odd to add a trace point w/o trace event in the \u0027events\u0027 folder, but I see your point.\n\nI suppose having a \u0027trace/hooks\u0027 folder might help a little bit keeping the hooks well separated. We could have, say, \u0027hooks/sched.h\u0027 for all sched hooks, without having to touch the upstream code in \u0027events/sched.h\u0027.",
      "parentUuid": "d73eda37_425fa12e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "0efbc6e50475a746d1bd05b91c10ae57308d6d63",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
